{"id":"H6165","lemma":"עָרַג","transliteration":"arag","sayIt":"a-rag","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to long for","meaning":"(Qal) to long for, pant after","glosses":["pants","pant"],"count":2,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"psa-42","v":1,"renderings":{"bsb":"pants","kjv":"panteth"}},{"chapterId":"jol-1","v":20,"renderings":{"bsb":"pant","kjv":"cry"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Psalm 42:1","note":"As the deer pants for the water brooks, so my soul pants after you, God.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Joel 1:20","note":"Yes, the animals of the field pant to you, for the water brooks have dried up, And the fire has devoured the pastures of the wilderness.","source":"web"}],"related":[],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}